docs/page-templates.md:75:Sections: Overview, Toxicology, Typical exposure routes, Food sources (linked to `ingredients/`), Regulatory limits (linked to `regulations/`), Testing (linked to `testing/`), Microbiome effects (linked to `microbiome/`), Vulnerable populations, Open questions, Sources.
docs/page-templates.md:117:Every non-stub ingredient page must carry these `## H2` headings in order. Stubs (all-pending `contamination_profile`, no contributing sources) are exempt. The lint check in CLAUDE.md Part 18 enforces these; failed pages surface via the `COMPLETE-INGREDIENT-SECTIONS` action.
docs/page-templates.md:121:3. `## Ranges by source, region, and variety` — geographic and varietal variation, anchored on sources.
docs/page-templates.md:122:4. `## Processing effects` — polishing, rinsing, parboiling, fermentation, drying, milling, refining. Cite the source for each claim.
docs/page-templates.md:124:6. `## Mitigation options` — practical interventions ordered by impact magnitude. Subsection order: sourcing → agronomic → processing → formulation → testing/QC → packaging/storage. Each lever is a one-paragraph entry naming the magnitude with a cited source. Cross-link to dedicated `mitigation/<topic>.md` pages.
docs/page-templates.md:126:8. `## Sources` — source legend table auto-generated by `tools/evidence/build-source-legend.mjs`.
docs/page-templates.md:128:Stub pages carry only sections 2 (body table, all rows marked data gap) and 8 (source legend with empty-corpus message). When a stub crosses two-plus contributing A-tier sources, the section-completion subprocess action drafts sections 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 from the routing audit and contributing source pages.
