docs/page-templates.md:164:- Each entry: `region` (or `period`), `range_ppb`, `n`, `sources` list, optional `note`.
docs/page-templates.md:184:`n_studies` is the count of A-tier or B-tier sources contributing values. `n_studies: 0` with `status: populated` is a legitimate finding: the literature is silent on this combination; the app should treat as data gap rather than "probably clean." `n_studies: 0` with `status: pending` is the template default.
docs/page-templates.md:190:When any ingest touches an ingredient page (advances at least one sub-block to `in_progress` or `populated`), all ten sub-blocks must move out of `pending` in the same pass. Sub-blocks the source does not cover advance to `status: populated, n_studies: 0, confidence: null, last_reviewed: <today>` — the declared-data-gap state. Mixed-state pages (some `populated`, some `pending`) are a lint failure. All-`pending` stubs (no ingest yet) are not lint failures; they are the legitimate stub state.
