docs/gpt-collaboration/system-prompt.md:81:matrices: [<bare strings; broad scope; see matrices guidance>]
docs/gpt-collaboration/system-prompt.md:119:2. FRONTMATTER SCOPE IS BROAD, NOT NARROW. If a paper measures "230 infant formulas" without specifying soy vs non-soy, frontmatter says products: ["[[products/infant-formula]]"] or matrices: [infant-formula] — NOT products: ["[[products/infant-formula-non-soy-powder]]"]. The routing layer fans broad scopes to sibling pages automatically. Overspecifying is worse than underspecifying. (If infant-formula is not in the snapshot's product list, follow rule 1: leave [] and add a verification note.)
docs/gpt-collaboration/system-prompt.md:155:11. WHEN UNCERTAIN, LEAVE BLANK. Empty fields are safe; guessed fields create downstream errors that are expensive to find later. If you do not know the DOI, write null. If you do not know the license, write "unknown." If sample_n is not stated, write null. If you cannot tell whether the matrix is breast milk or infant formula from the extracted text, leave matrices empty and flag it in verification notes.
docs/gpt-collaboration/system-prompt.md:167:Common matrices: rice, rice-flour, rice-cereal, infant-formula, infant-formula-powder, infant-formula-rtf, baby-food-puree, fruit-puree, vegetable-puree, baby-snack, cereal-grain, leafy-vegetable, root-vegetable, fish, shellfish, mollusk, seaweed, cocoa, chocolate, tea, coffee, drinking-water, breast-milk, cow-milk, soy-milk, plant-protein-powder, whey-protein, dietary-supplement, soil, sediment, blood, urine, hair, dietary-intake. Pick the broadest term that accurately describes what was measured. Add a new term only if none of these fits; flag the addition in verification notes.
docs/gpt-collaboration/verification-checklist.md:61:- **All slugs in `metals:`, `ingredients:`, `products:`, `matrices:`, `jurisdictions:`** exist in the current taxonomy. Cross-reference against `wiki/ingredients/`, `wiki/products/`, `wiki/metals/`, and the matrices vocabulary in `docs/gpt-collaboration/system-prompt.md`. Invented slugs → either correct to the right existing slug or set the field to `[]` and add to the verification notes for Karen.
docs/page-templates.md:26:matrices: [dietary-intake, urine, blood]
docs/page-templates.md:245:Row-fit is a compound classification with two axes: **matrix axis** (milk-based vs soy-based vs hydrolyzed; rice-based vs non-rice; root vegetable vs leafy green) and **format axis** (powdered vs ready-to-feed vs concentrated liquid; dry vs as-consumed; jar vs pouch). Each axis is exact, partial, or unknown independently. Source-page TL;DR and frontmatter `matrices` / `products` should record both axes explicitly when known.
docs/conventions.md:7:**Units:** Always ppb (µg/kg) for food matrices unless a source uses different units, in which case convert and note the original. Always specify wet weight vs dry weight.
docs/conventions.md:33:All other frontmatter array fields stay bare; they are tag/classifier vocabularies (`metals`, `jurisdictions`, `audience`, `species`, `drivers`, `aliases`, `mechanism`, `disease_links`, `matrices`, `applicable_regulations`, `typical_ingredients`, `near_duplicates`), not page references.
